From 511ca9253fdd1581d6c3eda2b6b968a47da1ac1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:53:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/23] runtime: pose_prediction = "measured" predicts the head
 pose to the time it is seen

The runtime predicted the head pose about 10 ms ahead (the server pipeline estimate),
while the sample reaches the eye about 34 ms after the client took it. The runtime now
measures that sample-to-display latency in the live chain and can use it as the horizon.

Measured, per frame, smoothed (EMA 0.1), logged every 5 s as
"StreamingServer: sample->display latency (measured)":
- sample age at fetch: now minus the receive time of the tracking sample WaitFrame used
- render: WaitFrame fetch to SendFrame
- encode+send: SendFrame to the last packet handed to the socket (and to send start)
- client displayed age: the client's own LatencyReport.displayedFrameAgeMs
- rtt: RttProbe, a 1 Hz probe thread (ICMP echo, else UDP port-unreachable). The protocol
  has no ping/pong and no clock sync. Inside Godot on the Mac every probe send is refused
  (No route to host / Broken pipe), so a fixed 5.3 ms is used and logged as assumed.

pose_prediction = "fixed" (default) keeps the old behaviour. "measured" sets the horizon
per call to (now - sample receive) + post-fetch latency, clamped to 0-60 ms, and falls
back to the fixed estimate until every term is measured. pose_prediction_horizon_ms > 0
overrides both with a constant.

TrackingReceiver also scores each frame's predicted pose against the client's later
samples at sample time + measured latency and logs the derived reprojection delta
(rot mean/p95, pos mean, and the unpredicted baseline) every 5 s.

The UDP probe socket sets SO_NOSIGPIPE and is reopened after any unanswered probe: an
earlier build without it took Godot down silently about a second after the switch to UDP.

Live, off-head, 60 s windows (bitrate 50, ffe medium, 90 Hz):
fixed:    horizon 10.0-10.3 ms, measured latency 33.1-34.6 ms
measured: horizon 32.9-36.2 ms, measured latency 33.7-35.7 ms
Reprojection delta 0.000 deg either way: the pose is still off-head.

Tests: [input] 211 assertions in 13 test cases pass, including a new measured-mode case.

